// expect: 0
// The first step of the route to the Daisy Seed (PLAN §11, "The order from
// 2026-11-12", N0): an ARM program made by hand, byte by byte.
// `mentl run native/exit42.mn > exit42.elf` writes 90 bytes, and
// `qemu-arm exit42.elf` exits 42 once the file may be run (`chmod +x`).
import io

import elf

// Thumb code: movs r0, #42; movs r7, #1; svc 0. Linux reads r7 as the call
// it is asked for, where 1 is exit, and r0 as the exit code.
fn code() = [42, 32, 1, 39, 0, 223]

fn main() = {
  code() |> linux_program |> print_string
  0
}
